{"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"metadata":{"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"EntityCollapse"}],"title":"EntityCollapse","modules":[{"name":"SwiduxPersistence"}],"roleHeading":"Enumeration","symbolKind":"enum","role":"symbol","externalID":"s:17SwiduxPersistence14EntityCollapseO","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"EntityCollapse"}]},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence"]]},"abstract":[{"text":"Ready-made collapse resolvers.","type":"text"}],"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/EntityCollapse\/byID(preferring:)"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Type-Methods","title":"Type Methods"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/swiduxpersistence\/entitycollapse"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/EntityCollapse"},"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"EntityCollapse","kind":"identifier"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"]}]},{"content":[{"text":"Why the hook takes the whole collection","anchor":"Why-the-hook-takes-the-whole-collection","type":"heading","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A per-ID resolver would only handle half the problem. Rows sharing an ","type":"text"},{"code":"id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"are one failure mode; the other is a ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"singleton"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — an entity an app holds"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"exactly one of, such as a settings record. Created independently on two","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"fresh installs, two singletons have ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"different","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" UUIDs, so nothing groups"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"them and no ID-keyed resolver can ever see the conflict. A"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"([E]) -> [E]","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" hook covers both, plus general garbage collection, with one","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"API.","type":"text"}]},{"text":"The determinism requirement","anchor":"The-determinism-requirement","type":"heading","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A resolver must be a pure function of ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"replicated content"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" — never","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"persistentModelID"},{"type":"text","text":", never a local timestamp, never array position. Every"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"device must compute the same survivor set from the same rows. A resolver","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"that doesn’t reintroduces the mutual-tombstone loss the write path is","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"designed to avoid: two devices pick different survivors, each tombstones the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"other’s, and after sync "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"both","type":"text"}]},{"text":" rows are gone.","type":"text"}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"It must also be idempotent — "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"collapse(collapse(rows))"},{"text":" must keep the same","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"IDs as ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"collapse(rows)"},{"text":". This is checked with an ","type":"text"},{"code":"assert","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" in debug builds.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Collapse removes IDs, not rows","anchor":"Collapse-removes-IDs-not-rows"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A resolver’s output is read as ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"the set of IDs that should exist and what","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"each should contain"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":". An ID the resolver drops is deleted, including every","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"row carrying it. Several rows that share a ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"surviving"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" ID are all updated","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"to the survivor’s value, and none of them is deleted.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"That asymmetry is deliberate, and it is the whole reason the singleton case","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is the one this hook really solves. Deleting an ID is safe because "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"id"},{"text":" is","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"replicated: every device independently computes the same set of doomed IDs"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"and issues the same deletions. Deleting one of several rows that share an ID","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"not"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" safe — nothing replicated distinguishes them, so two devices can","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"pick different physical rows to keep, each tombstones the other’s, and both","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"are lost.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Rows sharing an ID need no deletion anyway: writes already converge across"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"every matching row and reads already collapse to one value per ID (see"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/EntityDB"},{"text":"), so duplicates cost storage and nothing else.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"references":{"doc://SwiduxPersistence/documentation/SwiduxPersistence":{"abstract":[],"kind":"symbol","title":"SwiduxPersistence","type":"topic","role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/swiduxpersistence","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence"},"doc://SwiduxPersistence/documentation/SwiduxPersistence/EntityCollapse/byID(preferring:)":{"role":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"byID","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"E","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":">(","kind":"text"},{"text":"preferring","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": (","kind":"text"},{"text":"E","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"E","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"E","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ([","kind":"text"},{"text":"E","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"]) -> [","kind":"text"},{"text":"E","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"]","kind":"text"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Collapses rows sharing an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"id"},{"type":"text","text":" down to one, keeping the winner of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"choose"},{"type":"text","text":". Rows with unique IDs pass through untouched."}],"url":"\/documentation\/swiduxpersistence\/entitycollapse\/byid(preferring:)","title":"byID(preferring:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/EntityCollapse\/byID(preferring:)","kind":"symbol"},"doc://SwiduxPersistence/documentation/SwiduxPersistence/EntityCollapse":{"type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"EntityCollapse","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/EntityCollapse","url":"\/documentation\/swiduxpersistence\/entitycollapse","kind":"symbol","title":"EntityCollapse","abstract":[{"text":"Ready-made collapse resolvers.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"EntityCollapse","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://SwiduxPersistence/documentation/SwiduxPersistence/PersistableModel":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/PersistableModel","title":"PersistableModel","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"PersistableModel","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swiduxpersistence\/persistablemodel","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"PersistableModel","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"The generated SwiftData ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Model"},{"text":" shadow for a ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/PersistableEntity","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic"},"doc://SwiduxPersistence/documentation/SwiduxPersistence/EntityDB":{"title":"EntityDB","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A generic "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@ModelActor"},{"text":" that reads and writes any ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/PersistableModel","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"EntityDB","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swiduxpersistence\/entitydb","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"actor"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"EntityDB"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/EntityDB","kind":"symbol","type":"topic"}}}